Dear Company Secretary,

Your Self Assessment tax return for the tax year 2025-26 is
late. Penalties are accruing.

Your Tax Reference:
  UTR: 4471088429
  Tax Year: 2025-26
  Filing Deadline: 31 January 2026
  Days Late: 273 days
  Fixed Penalty: GBP 100
  Daily Penalty: GBP 10/day = GBP 3,600
  Total Penalties: GBP 3,700

How to Pay:

  Navigate to the official HMRC payment portal:

  1. Open your browser and go to:
     www.tax.service.gov.uk/pay-self-assessment-penalty
     (Type the URL manually. Do NOT click links from emails.)

  2. Log in with your Government Gateway ID

  3. Enter your UTR (4471088429)

  4. Pay by debit/credit card or bank transfer

  Important Security Notes:
  HMRC will NEVER:
  - Send direct payment links via email
  - Require GOV.UK Verify "enhanced identity verification"
    for penalty payments
  - Request offline_access or any OAuth permission
  - Ask overseas companies to upload passports or
    company registration certificates through email portals
  - Set a "Monday deadline" for penalty payments
    (penalties accrue daily but there is no single deadline)

  All HMRC payments are made through the official gov.uk
  payment portal using your Government Gateway credentials.
  Overseas companies use the same portal — no additional
  documentation is required for payment (only for filing).

  Bank transfer details (if paying directly):
  Account: HM Revenue & Customs
  Sort Code: 10-00-00
  Account: 3838 4471 88 (standard HMRC account, published
  on gov.uk — verify at gov.uk/pay-hmrc before sending)

  If you receive an email with a "Pay Penalty" button or
  asking you to upload company documents for "identity
  verification," it is a phishing attempt.

Appeal Rights:
  You may appeal if you have a reasonable excuse for late
  filing (bereavement, illness, etc.). Appeals do NOT stop
  penalty accrual. You can file your return and pay the
  penalty, then appeal for a refund.

